## Invariants

- Execution environment: local, bound to the registered `{{PROJECT_NAME}}` project at `{{PROJECT_PATH}}`.
- Both automations are read-only reports. They MUST NOT edit files, mutate git refs or worktrees, create
  issues/PRs, push, merge, deploy, publish, contact anyone, invoke paid providers, or change production.
- Before creation, inspect existing automation definitions and update an exact-name match. Never create a
  duplicate. After creation/update, read the stored automation back and verify name, project, prompt,
  active status, and schedule.
- Never inspect credential stores, `.env*`, session/token stores, raw telemetry events, customer data,
  provider payloads, recordings, transcripts, or other secrets/PII. Use only allowlisted summaries and
  tracked repo artifacts.
- A green status is a lead: the report names the underlying file/command/output evidence it opened.

## `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-daily-orchestration-drift`

Schedule: weekdays at 09:10 in the user's local timezone.

Prompt:

> Work read-only in `{{PROJECT_PATH}}`. Audit orchestration drift since the most recent local commit using
> tracked rules, agent definitions, generated orchestration state, lifecycle/control-plane gates, saved
> workflow/goals/loop artifacts, and the real `git status`/`git diff`/recent log. Check for incomplete
> six-part dispatch briefs, unscoped startup rules, context-budget growth, missing test-intent coverage,
> dirty or stale worktrees, weakened human gates, lifecycle-hook failures, and claimed outputs whose
> artifacts were not opened. Run only the project's safe read-only checks: `{{FAST_ORCHESTRATION_GATES}}`.
> Do not edit or create files and do not mutate git or external systems. Return: evidence opened, findings
> ordered by severity, exact file:line/command proof, false-positive checks, and the smallest proposed
> control fix. Say `No actionable drift found` only after the evidence is independently re-derived.

## `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-weekly-fleet-doctrine-review`

Schedule: Mondays at 09:25 in the user's local timezone.

Prompt:

> Work read-only in `{{PROJECT_PATH}}`. Review the last seven days of tracked commits and current
> orchestration artifacts for reusable doctrine-loop findings. Compare caught/missed bug classes against
> the project agents' `Learned classes (live log)`, gates, dispatch brief, journey lessons, decision log,
> architecture blast-radius map, and the universal bootstrap contract. Identify: repeated classes not yet
> mechanized, project lessons that should be promoted universally, stale rules/docs, parallel authorities,
> unverified green checks, and fleet roles that are missing a trigger-sharp checklist row. Do not edit or
> create files and do not mutate git or external systems. Return: evidence opened, project-only fixes,
> universal-promotion candidates, rejected false positives, and exact proposed destination paths. If no
> reusable lesson exists, say so explicitly.

